A||N||1||Ozzy||The Blue Beast lives!!!||||10||
Z||000000||Ozzy||04-10-2000||12:47 AM||||Hi Humans...<P>Well, I finally got the exhaust manifolds on and patched up the exhaust system today! Somehow the cat. converter fell off and was replaced by a shiny new piece of 2" pipe.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>I also put new platinum plugs and wires with rotor and cap. The old ones were thrashed. I figured while I had all the stuff off the back of the engine and the decklid off...<P>Bunches of the connectors are hammered too. Spent some time cleaning up wiring and such.<P>So late today I had it all put back together and fired it up. Does not sound like a Cessna anymore!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> It sounds pretty damn Kool! No leaks...(yet) So I pulled it out of the drive way and took a test run...<B>WHHHEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE</B> 1st, 2nd, 3rd and <B>BOOOOOOM</B> (Sonic Boom that is!) 4th, and 5th. Being that I was at Wharp factor 3 I started backing off some and called the Seatac tower to get landing clearance   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  <P>O.K. so I got a LITTLE carried away   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Point I'm trying to make is it definatley boogies for a stock engine. I can see lottsa potential with this car down the road. It still handles like a sack of custard but I will get it all ironed out soon enough.<P>Enough raving about my new toy...Just had to let it all out.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||10
Z||000001||iplayazi||04-10-2000||01:06 AM||||Sniff. That was beautiful.. hehe glad it went well man. I know what you mean about piping the cat..I had to change the starter and the alternater  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||12
